meta {
  name: 400
  seq: 5
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer token-one, Bearer token-two
  X-Authorization: Bearer placeholder-token
  X-Service-Name: bruno-test
}

docs {
  # 400 Bad Request (Ambiguous/Malformed Auth Headers)

  `AuthHeaderValidationFilter` runs ahead of Spring Security and
  rejects any request whose `Authorization` or `X-Authorization` header is duplicated,
  comma-joined or otherwise not exactly one `Bearer <token>` value. The header override above
  sends a comma-joined `Authorization` value, so every request in this folder should be rejected
  with `400 Bad Request` (`application/problem+json`) before authentication is even attempted —
  no valid token is required, and the response does not say which header/check failed.
}
